examples.en:
She made an appontment with me in Sangzhong;
She will meet me in Shanggong;
She will accompany me to Qishang.

What dreams are lucky?
They have been about black bears and brown bears;
They have been about asps and adders.

Sailing seas depends on the helmsman;
Life and growth depend on the sun;
Rain and dewdrops nourish the crops;
Making revolution depends on Mao Zedong Thought.

In the east there is Lucifer;
In the west there is Hesperus;
Long and curved is the Rabbit Net of the sky; -
But they only occupy their places.

In the brook below the hill there drowns the orchid bud;
The sandy path between pine-trees shows not a trace of mud;
And cuckoos cry, in mournful rain.

Sailing seas depends on the helmsman;
Life and growth depend on the sun;
Rain and dewdrops nourish the crops;
Making revolution depends on Mao Zedong Thought.

Around the bed run hungry rats;
In lamplight to and fro fly bats.
On pine-shaded roof the wind and shower rattle;
The window paper scraps are heard to prattle.

In the ninth month, about the doors;
In the tenth month, the cricket enters under our beds.
Chinks are filled up, and rats are smoked out.
The windows that face [the north] are stopped up;

In the east there is Lucifer;
In the west there is Hesperus;
Long and curved is the Rabbit Net of the sky; -
But they only occupy their places.
